# Flexbox: A Comprehensive Guide

This document summarizes the core concepts and properties of CSS Flexbox, based on the video tutorial "Learn CSS Flexbox in 20 Minutes."

## What is Flexbox?

Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system that helps you arrange and align items within a single row or column. It's a powerful tool for creating dynamic, responsive designs.

## Fundamental Concepts

### 1. The Main and Cross Axes

Flexbox is based on two axes that determine how items are positioned:
* **Main Axis:** The primary direction in which flex items are laid out (e.g., left-to-right).
* **Cross Axis:** The axis perpendicular to the main axis (e.g., top-to-bottom).

### 2. Centering Items

A common use case for Flexbox is centering an element both horizontally and vertically with just a few lines of code.

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center; /* Aligns along the main axis */
  align-items: center;     /* Aligns along the cross axis */
}
````

-----

## Flexbox Properties

Properties are divided into two categories: those for the parent container and those for the child items.

### Parent Container Properties

These are applied to the element you want to turn into a flex container.

| Property | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `display: flex;` | Initializes the flex container and enables Flexbox for its direct children. |
| `flex-direction` | Controls the direction of the main axis (`row`, `column`, `row-reverse`, `column-reverse`). |
| `justify-content` | Aligns items along the **main axis**. Useful values: `center`, `flex-start`, `space-between`, `space-around`, `space-evenly`. |
| `align-items` | Aligns items along the **cross axis**. Values: `center`, `flex-start`, `flex-end`, `stretch`. |
| `flex-wrap` | Specifies whether items should wrap to a new line when they run out of space. Essential for responsive design. |
| `gap` | Defines the space between flex items, both horizontally and vertically. |

### Child Item Properties

These are applied to the direct children of a flex container.

| Property | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `flex-grow` | Controls how much an item will grow to fill available space (e.g., `flex-grow: 1`). |
| `flex-shrink` | Controls how an item will shrink to prevent overflow. |
| `flex-basis` | Sets the initial size of an item before any growing or shrinking occurs. |
| `flex` | A shorthand property for `flex-grow`, `flex-shrink`, and `flex-basis`. Example: `flex: 1 1 0%`. |

